# HEM-7156T: first-time pairing (key registration), read history, end the session.
name hem-7156t/pair
flow pair
advertise name=BLEsmart_0000057A0011223344 services=ecbe3980-c9a2-11e1-b1bd-0002a5d5c51b
# Synthetic Device Information; Omron reads the revisions and the System ID during connection setup.
dis model=HEM-7156T firmware=0001 software=0001 systemid=0011223344556677
time 2026-01-02T03:04:05 zone=UTC
key 05050505050505050505050505050505

alias unlock b305b680-aee7-11e1-a730-0002a5d5c51b
alias tx db5b55e0-aee7-11e1-965e-0002a5d5c51b,e0b8a060-aee7-11e1-92f4-0002a5d5c51b,0ae12b00-aee8-11e1-a192-0002a5d5c51b,10e1ba60-aee8-11e1-89e5-0002a5d5c51b
alias rx 49123040-aee8-11e1-a74d-0002a5d5c51b,4d0bf320-aee8-11e1-a0d9-0002a5d5c51b,5128ce60-aee8-11e1-b84b-0002a5d5c51b,560f1420-aee8-11e1-8184-0002a5d5c51b
alias clock 00002a2b-0000-1000-8000-00805f9b34fb

# Same synthetic record and index as hem-7156t/connect-read-history.
memory fill=ff
memory 0x98 694e4319261da603 0000 0100 00000000
memory 0x10 0100 0000 0100 0000 01000000

# Enter key mode, program the key.
write unlock 02 00000000000000000000000000000000
notify unlock 8200
write unlock 00 05050505050505050505050505050505
notify unlock 8000
# OpenPressure follows the pinned omblepy order and unlocks with the new key.
[ours-only: Omron does not follow registration with 01 (docs/protocol.md, observed in the sandbox)] write unlock 01 05050505050505050505050505050505
[ours-only: acknowledgment for the unlock above] notify unlock 8100

write tx 08 00 00 00 00 10 00 18
notify rx 18 80 00 00 00 10 00 01 02 03 04 05 06 07 08 09 0a 0b 0c 0d 0e 0f 00 88

[omron-only: Omron reads the HEM-7156T_AP index block (index_setting_read_address) before records] reads 0x10 44 chunk=44
[omron-only: Omron reads setting-info block 3 (index_setting_info_read_address 0x20 + 28)] reads 0x3c 16 chunk=16

[ours-only: index-driven populated-slot read: OpenPressure reads the 68-byte settings/index image at 0x10 in 56-byte blocks, then only the slots it lists as populated; Omron reads 44 bytes plus block 3 and then only unsent records] reads 0x10 68 chunk=56

[ours-only: index-driven populated-slot read: OpenPressure imports the populated slots during Pair; Omron pairing flags 0x1210 return settings without historical readings (observed in the sandbox)] reads 0x98 16 chunk=48

# Omron Connect 2026.09.03 post-transfer settings frames, recorded against this synthetic fixture.
# Replies are synthetic full echoes; no physical monitor's acknowledgment is established.
[omron-only: Omron 2026.09.03 post-transfer index prefix at 0x54, with the last-read user's cleared unsent counter and birthday block 1; docs/omron-sandbox.md] write tx 2601c000541e 010000000080000001000000ffffffff000101fffffffffffffffffff9ff 00d4
[omron-only: synthetic full echo acknowledgment; the physical monitor reply is unconfirmed] notify rx 2681c000541e 010000000080000001000000ffffffff000101fffffffffffffffffff9ff 0054
[omron-only: Omron 2026.09.03 settings at 0x80, block 3 clock (fixture time + 1 s); docs/omron-sandbox.md] write tx 1801c0008010 ffffffffffffffff1a010203040622ff 008c
[omron-only: synthetic full echo acknowledgment; the physical monitor reply is unconfirmed] notify rx 1881c0008010 ffffffffffffffff1a010203040622ff 000c

# Both clients use the normal END after completing their respective steps.
write tx 08 0f 00 00 00 00 00 07
notify rx 08 8f 00 00 00 00 00 87

[ours-only: OpenPressure imports history during Pair; Omron 0x1210 returns no historical readings] expect reading user=1 sys=130 dia=78 pulse=67 time=2025-07-09T06:14:38
